{
  "name": "done_state_propagation",
  "description": "Entering a final state raises done.state for its compound parent only; then, while the next ancestor is a parallel state whose regions are all in final states, done.state for that parallel state (a history child is not a region). No other ancestor is notified: a compound grandparent whose child completed (a.b) does not complete, so aDone never runs. Every raised done.state event is processed, in order; one without an onDone handler reaches the root's wildcard (anyRoot), which makes it observable.",
  "tags": [
    "final",
    "onDone",
    "parallel",
    "history",
    "wildcard"
  ],
